Z||000000||JetroGT||03-23-2000||04:12 PM||||I had posted earler that I was restoring an 87 blue GT that was hit in the front. It's almost done! I went to the shop today. The front is all repainted along with the doors to blend the paint. I had everything cut off just in front of the front compartment and a new front welded in. New fenders, hood, front cover, radiator, condenser, and a new left headlight frame. <BR>I always wanted a blue GT. <BR>5spd, pw, pl, pm, sub, cruse, no sunroof  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Now all I need is a V8!||||reg||6
Z||000001||sdm1964||03-23-2000||09:34 PM||||Cool beans man, But you know it is manditory that you post pics when finished. I love that blue, My next GT will be blue or red can't decide. Got to be an aero back. can't wait to see.||||reg||14
Z||000002||bHooper||03-23-2000||10:14 PM||||yes, you must post some photo's!  and i am jealouse!  i start the major road back, on my GT, next weekend with the new tranny!<P>congrats!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||03-25-2000||08:46 PM||||I got the GT back today. Got it in the drive way and changed the front brakes. pads rotors and berings.<BR>I took it for a test drive on the interstate and what do you know, I'm leaving a white vapor trail. But only after reving high then shifting up. Looks like I'll be changing the head gaskets. <BR>Has anyone ever done this with the engine in the car? I have all the tools to do it but just haven't done it before. Any one have any pointers they would like to share?||||reg||8
Z||000004||AL||03-25-2000||09:03 PM||||be prepaired to hurt at the waist,actually it's all pretty simple,get a can of folgers and put all bolts in there, so you don't lose any as far as tips well you just have to take it all off, there is nothing else i can tell you,but when you do have everything off make sure you clean the inside of the plenum and the intermediate intake manifold and lower manifold, get all the gunk that is in there, and after you have put it all together be carefull with connecting the fuel block up to the fuel lines it strips out very easy, and replace all o rings and if you have the money replace all injectors, if not just put oil on the o rings or w40 before you snap them backin. that's it, good luck and go slow, buy some bengay for your back just in case lol,AL.||||reg||14
Z||000005||JetroGT||03-26-2000||01:41 AM||||Thanks. Thats pretty much what I thought. Right now I'm stripping an extra pair of valve covers. I also have an extra lower plenum that I can prep, along with a set of heads from when I did my SE. At least this way I know it will have a good top end. <P>Should I leave everything red, or paint it blue to match the car? I think the blue would stand out more at a show.||||reg||1
